# Build context for the parser sidecar only (BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore
# in preference to .dockerignore). The app's .dockerignore excludes scripts/ to keep
# the Next.js image lean, which would leave this image with no source at all.
#
# Allowlist, not a denylist: everything is excluded and the parser files are
# added back, so no .env, no app source and no node_modules can reach this image.
*
!scripts/parse_statements.py
!scripts/statement_service.py
!scripts/parser-requirements.txt
!scripts/parser-requirements.lock
!scripts/bank_detect.py
!scripts/l10n_keywords.py
